div.div:
@yearnaudov thanks for the detailed report and the stress-testing. It was very useful. All four points are addressed in v1.3.0 (pip install -U bg-text-normalizer):
два/две: 2 коли now gives две коли, and 2 компютъра stays два. Minus sign: -12 градуса gives минус дванадесет градуса. Scores like 3-2 are read as a range, not as "минус". Latin No: No 15 and No. 15 give номер петнадесет. It only applies before a digit, so No way is untouched. Roman numerals: these are opt-in, as you suggested. Use BulgarianTextNormalizer(roman_numerals=True) and Карл V becomes Карл пети. A lone C, D, L or M after a name is skipped, since it is usually an initial.
Decimals like -5,5 are read as "пет цяло и пет", not "пет цяло и пет десети". That is intentional, so I've left it as is. Closing this. Feel free to open a new issue if you find anything else.
